  "$comment": "Backward design. Nothing gets written until this exists. The bank is MEASURED against this file per standard, per DOK, per item type, and drift fails in EITHER direction. Writing items first and describing the coverage afterward produces a bank that is 70% DOK-1 recall and reads as complete.",
  "blueprintVersion": 1,
  "course": "us-history-geography",
  "standardsPrefix": "US",
  "standardsYear": "2027-28",
  "status": "OPERATING TARGET — adopted by the build so authoring can proceed; not signed off by the course owner. release-readiness HOLDS while this reads 'operating' or 'draft'. Raise or lower it freely: the bank is measured against this file, and blueprint-conformance fails in BOTH directions, so a target set too high never goes green.",
  "rationale": {
    "itemCount": "6 per standard = enough to build two non-overlapping 3-item forms per standard.",
    "dokSpread": "2/2/1/1 puts 33% at DOK-1. The failure mode this resists is a bank that drifts to 70% recall; the gate fails a standard that is over OR under on any level.",
    "itemType": "4 selected-response + 1 constructed + 1 document-based keeps a DBQ tier on every standard."
  },
